{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Am I in the place of Elohim.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'Am I in His place, that I should have power to attend to barrenness? And this key was not given into the hand of a messenger.' And this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: three keys were not given into the hand of a messenger, and they are: the key of childbirth, the key of rains, and the key of the revival of the dead. And therefore he said: התחת אלהים אנכי — 'Am I in the place of Elohim' — am I in His place, or am I His messenger, that I should give you what He has withheld from you?'" "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah, התחת אלהים אנכי — I have already hinted at it above, at the beginning of the parashah. And the ה of התחת is not a interrogative heh but a certitude heh, like (1 Samuel 2:27) הנגלה נגלתי, and it is as if he said: תחת ה׳ — 'in place of YHWH' — who is Elohim, אנכי. He informed her that his image is engraved in the merkavah, and from this he knows that Elohim is the One who withholds; and therefore she pressed herself to give him Bilhah her maidservant, in order to draw the power of childbirth from her through the power of the ה, which is Elohim the Withholder, and to Him she prayed in the end, as it is written: ״ויזכר אלהים את רחל וישמע אליה אלהים״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The phrase 'והלא מפתח זה לא נמסר ביד שליח' appears to be Jacob paraphrasing the rabbinic dictum before Rabbenu Bahya cites it formally; rendered in single quotes to mark the embedded paraphrase."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:27.735326854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}